 CO3.2  COMPARISON
==============================================================================
   Policy        Placed  Rejected   Largest hole  Stranded MB   Verdict
   First-Fit          7         0          2,004           94      best
   Best-Fit           7         0          2,800          354          
   Worst-Fit          6         1          2,000            0          

   Reading of the result:
   - Best-Fit leaves the smallest leftovers, which is exactly why it
     manufactures slivers of memory too small to host any guest.
   - Worst-Fit preserves large holes but consumes the big ones early,
     so the last large request is the one that gets rejected.
   - First-Fit is O(1) amortised in search cost and, on this workload,
     places the same number of guests as Best-Fit. For a hypervisor
     admitting VMs on a hot path, search cost is not free.

